he police this week i won't be  doing that  um on patrol i have seen almost every  week and on a daily basis  the police in action and engage in the  public around coronavirus  the public are really sensible actually  i spoke to the head of the police  federation just yesterday who said  he and his members have not yet received  the guidance from uh from central  government  as to what they are supposed to be  correct but that that  that is what he said so the guidance  went out on sunday night at seven  o'clock  and i know because i was involved in  that we were working obviously  throughout the weekend  with the mpcc in fact to oversee the  guidance that goes out to all police  forces  so you know the police operate on the  guidance but i think it's important to  emphasize  the police have quite a clear playbook  now when it comes to the four e's  speaking to the public engaging  explaining encouraging  enforcement is the last resort but you  know they have the tools such as fixed  penalty fines  um they go after egregious breaches we  spoke about some religious breaches last  week as well  and it's important that the police  continue to do that they'll be as  visible as they have been across our  communities  is there any chance that we will be  hearing from this government  before christmas any changes to the  current tier system  well i think first of all we have a set  timetable in terms of review periods  we also we also changed that for london  but also let me let me just say as well  you know  we keep everything under review you know  you hear from the government every day  you have ministers here with you  certainly every single morning you know  my colleagues no doubt will keep  you and all your viewers updated in  terms of you know the spread of the  virus  but also a reminder of the protective  measures that we can undertake to keep  each other safe  and we will let you go but just one last  question i mean it's it's been pretty  definitively ruled out 